positorio.imarpe.gob.pe/items/ccaf8326-3072-429e-be44-1be36234fb3d)\nciteturn12search2 [wordlim: 200] Published: 11.8 years ago; Crawled: last week; Some 290 species of squids comprise the order Teuthida that belongs to the molluscan Class Cephalopoda. ... Calamar, Pesca, Artes de pesca, Captura ... P., Guerra, A., Hendrickson,...\n\n# World Squid Fisheries\n\n## Archivos\n\nPrincipal World Squid Fisheries.pdf (8.26 MB)\n\n## Fecha\n\n2015\n\n## Autores\n\nArkhipkin, Alexander I.\n\nRodhouse, Paul G. K.\n\nPierce, Graham J.\n\nSauer, Warwick\n\nSakai, Mitsuo\n\nAllcock, Louise\n\nArgüelles Torres, Juan\n\nBower, John R.\n\nCastillo, Gladis\n\nCeriola, Luca\n\n[Button: Mostrar 10 más]\n\n## Editor\n\nTaylor and Francis Group\n\n## Resumen\n\nSome 290 species of squids comprise the order Teuthida that belongs to the molluscan Class Cephalopoda. Of these, about 30-40 squid species have substantial commercial importance around the world. Squid fisheries make a rather small contribution to world landings from capture fisheries relative to that of fish, but the proportion has increased steadily over the last decade, with some signs of recent leveling off. The present overview describes all substantial squid fisheries around the globe. The main ecological and biological features of exploited stocks, and key aspects of fisheries management are presented for each commercial species of squid worldwide. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nINSTITUTO DEL MAR DEL PERÚ (https://revistas.imarpe.gob.pe/index.php/boletin/issue/download/12/27-1-2)\nciteturn12search12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 12.8 years ago; Malacostraca- Eucarida. ... simpátricas de cangrejos ermitaños Pagurus (Decapoda, ... decápodos y estomatópodos del Perú. ... Manual de identificação dos crustaceos Decapoda\nBol Inst Mar Perú, 27 / Nos. 1 y 2 / Enero - Diciembre 2012\nISSN0458-7766\nHiller A, Lazarus Jr, Werding B. 2004. New records and \ncific Ocean (Crustacea: